,{},"Redirect to ",[500,978,979],{},"$url",". Each call returns a fresh time-bounded link; do not cache it. Redirect defaults come from configuration, and the array can override ",[500,982,983],{},"redirectUrlSuccess"," and ",[500,986,987],{},"redirectUrlCanceled",". Missing URLs raise ",[500,990,991],{},"IncompleteInformationException",[496,993,994,995,998,999,1002],{},"The ",[500,996,997],{},"subscription.billing_updated"," reaction refreshes the locally stored mandate summary. The ",[724,1000,1001],{"href":219},"customer portal"," is an alternative for broader self-service billing.",[513,1004,1006],{"id":1005},"read-local-state-carefully","Read local state carefully",[496,1008,1009,632,1012,636,1015,1018,1019,1022,1023,861],{},[500,1010,1011],{},"isValid()",[500,1013,1014],{},"isOnGracePeriod()",[500,1016,1017],{},"isEnded()"," delegate to your local model. They are only as current as your webhook handling. The optional ",[500,1020,1021],{},"DerivesSubscriptionState"," trait derives them from the end date, not payment status. Handle payment recovery and entitlement rules explicitly; see ",[724,1024,1025],{"href":226},"Event flow",[1027,1028,1029],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html pre.shiki code .s2Zo4, html code.shiki .s2Zo4{--shiki-light:#6182B8;--shiki-default:#82AAFF;--shiki-dark:#82AAFF}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html .light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style);font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight);text-decoration: var(--shiki-light-text-decoration);}html.light .shiki span {color: var(--shiki-light);background: var(--shiki-light-bg);font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style